CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT macro
#93: FILE: drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c:53:
+#define MT_QUIRK_SERIAL_REPORT_MODE	(1 << 7)

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around '!td->last_field_index'
#119: FILE: drivers/hid/hid-multitouch.c:204:
+	if ((quirks & MT_QUIRK_SERIAL_REPORT_MODE) &&
+		(!td->last_field_index))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

